' NIGHT ROUNDS
' An original game by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio,
' 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu: a ray-cast museum on a ColecoVision.
'
' The game: you are the night guard of a small museum. A thief is inside,
' going from gallery to gallery and cutting paintings out of their frames.
' Listen for his footsteps (louder when he is near, quicker and sharper
' when he runs), find him and catch him by walking into him. Your torch
' shows him (and the paintings) from afar, but he sees its beam and runs;
' in the dark you only see him close by. Each night the museum is bigger,
' the thief quicker and your spare batteries fewer. If he gets away with
' the night's limit of paintings, the game is over.
'
' Controls (either joystick): up walks, down steps back, left and right
' turn; a tap of the button switches the torch on or off; hold the button
' for the plan of the museum. Keypad not used.
'
' How it is drawn: The Stacks' ray caster (gen.py, ray_src.asm -> ray.asm),
' with its first textured walls: a ray that meets a painting's wall face
' gets the painting's texel tiles for its column, on as many rows as the
' painting is tall at that distance (painting tiles live in the middle
' screen third, rows 8-15, around the horizon). The thief is a scaled,
' magnified sprite whose 8-pixel columns are cut where a wall is nearer
' (the ray caster's depth buffer Zc).
'
' House rules kept: text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22; the frame loop is
' protected from the NMI and every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a
' wait. Menus by joystick (START, HOW TO PLAY, CREDITS); an original title
' tune that plays once; one press at game over returns to the title.

